cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
title: >-
  Analysis code for "Perceptibility of Error Outcomes Determines the
  Direction of Post-Error Adjustment"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived values for a study of post-error adjustment in
  online chess. Two kinds of error are identified independently in the same
  games - moves an engine scores as large evaluation drops, and moves after
  which material disappears from the board - and the direction of the
  subsequent change in decision time differs between them. The repository
  holds the full pipeline and the derived statistics behind every reported
  value. The code is under the MIT licence; the derived tables in
  data/derived/ are under CC BY 4.0.
